1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:05,492
Your N V M e drive is about thirteen times faster than a Sata S S D.

2
00:00:05,772 --> 00:00:07,967
So why don't your games load any faster?

3
00:00:08,717 --> 00:00:12,512
Sata tops out around 550 megabytes per second.

4
00:00:12,792 --> 00:00:21,048
A P C I e four drive, like Samsung's 990 Pro, is rated at 7,450.

5
00:00:21,798 --> 00:00:29,695
Yet in TechSpot's tests, a Cyberpunk save reloaded in about the same time on every S S D, Sata included.

6
00:00:29,975 --> 00:00:34,759
Starfield loaded less than a second apart on P C I e five and three.

7
00:00:35,509 --> 00:00:37,716
The drive isn't the slow part anymore.

8
00:00:37,996 --> 00:00:41,934
Your processor still has to unpack the files and build the level.

9
00:00:42,684 --> 00:00:47,052
Games using Direct Storage hand that unpacking to the graphics card.

10
00:00:47,332 --> 00:00:49,990
For most others, any S S D is enough.

11
00:00:50,740 --> 00:00:56,389
The full race is in our video, S S D versus H D D versus N V M e.

